 "customerTurns": 4,
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Samsung WD90T534DBW washer dryer - clothes are still damp at the end of the wash and dry programme. It's not that old. Is the heater going?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I cannot determine if the heater is working without performing specific electrical tests, which are unsafe to do yourself. You should contact a qualified appliance repair technician to diagnose and test the heating element safely. From what you have described, the most likely cause is a drying load bigger than the dry capacity. Does it get hot during drying but leave the clothes damp, or is there no heat at all - and were the clothes properly spun before the drying stage?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "It does get hot during drying and the clothes are warm at the end, just damp. I often turn the spin down to 800 to reduce creasing, so they weren't spun at full speed. It's a full 9kg drum, washed and dried in one go."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "A washer-dryer can only dry about half the load it washes — for example 8 kg wash / 5 kg dry. Drying a full wash load leaves it damp, and that's the most common cause. Check the dry capacity on the front or in the manual. Was the load more than the dry capacity (and have you split it), or was it within the dry capacity?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "The manual says 6kg for drying, so yes, I'm over that with a full 9kg drum and I haven't split it. Is that really enough to explain it?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, overloading the machine with a full 9kg load when the manual specifies only 6kg for drying is sufficient to leave clothes damp. The appliance cannot effectively dry more laundry than its rated capacity allows in a single cycle. Next: Try a SMALLER dry load - a washer-dryer dries less than it washes. Let me know what you find."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I tried a half drum with full spin and it came out dry. So I should just split the loads and use full spin, I take it?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Good news, that has sorted it. If it happens again, start with the same check. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  }
 ],
